18949:The draw:text-areas attribute specifies up to two text areas. If the attribute specifies one text area, this text area is used to position and align the text. If the attribute specifies two text areas, the second text area is used if a style that is assigned to the text has a style:writing-mode 20.404 attribute with value tb-rl or tb. Otherwise, the first text area is used. If the draw:text-areas attribute is omitted, the entire area of the shape is used to position and align the text. 

